{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018c7XEJSJ4cqRbP7aEFfJ8s","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# docs/TICKER_SCHEMA.md\n2\t\n3\tColumn dictionary for the planned `data/state/master_tickers.csv` (produced by\n4\t`build_master_tickers.py`). **No file exists yet** — this is the contract the\n5\tfuture script will write.\n6\t\n7\tOne row per distinct ticker across all `data/exports/*_clean.csv` files.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Columns (26)\n12\t\n13\t| # | Column | Type | Definition | Example |\n14\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n15\t| 1 | `ticker` | str | Uppercased ticker symbol, `$` stripped, deduped. | `MU` |\n16\t| 2 | `main_theme` | str | Most common theme across this ticker's posts (see `SCORING.md`). | `memory` |\n17\t| 3 | `sub_theme` | str | Second most common theme (or empty). | `AI infra` |\n18\t| 4 | `accounts_mentioning` | int | Total distinct accounts (strong + other) that mentioned it. | `4` |\n19\t| 5 | `mentions_photonbull` | int | # posts by `photonbull` mentioning it. | `3` |\n20\t| 6 | `mentions_ckcapitalxx` | int | # posts by `ckcapitalxx`. | `2` |\n21\t| 7 | `mentions_bryzonx` | int | # posts by `bryzonx`. | `0` |\n22\t| 8 | `mentions_frenchie` | int | # posts by `frenchie`. | `1` |\n23\t| 9 | `mentions_rjccapital` | int | # posts by `rjccapital`. | `5` |\n24\t| 10 | `mentions_other_accounts` | int | # posts by accounts not in the strong set. | `2` |\n25\t| 11 | `total_mentions` | int | Total posts (across all accounts) mentioning it. | `13` |\n26\t| 12 | `recent_mentions_7d` | int | Posts in the last 7 days (vs run date). | `2` |\n27\t| 13 | `recent_mentions_30d` | int | Posts in the last 30 days. | `6` |\n28\t| 14 | `avg_engagement` | float | Mean per-post `engagement_score` for this ticker. | `42.7` |\n29\t| 15 | `max_engagement` | int | Max single-post `engagement_score`. | `311` |\n30\t| 16 | `dominant_post_type` | str | Modal `post_type_guess` (`original`/`reply`/`retweet`/`quote`). | `original` |\n31\t| 17 | `conviction_global_1_to_5` | int | 1–5 conviction blend (thesis + recency + engagement). | `4` |\n32\t| 18 | `short_term_signal` | bool | Any post flagged `short_term_signal`. | `True` |\n33\t| 19 | `long_term_thesis` | bool | Any post flagged `long_term_thesis`. | `True` |\n34\t| 20 | `catalyst` | bool | Any post has `has_catalyst_language`. | `True` |\n35\t| 21 | `thesis_one_liner` | str | Best single representative post text (truncated). | `HBM cycle + MU earnings ...` |\n36\t| 22 | `convergence_level` | int | 1–5 from distinct strong-account count (see `SCORING.md`). | `4` |\n37\t| 23 | `signal_independence` | int | Distinct accounts (all) mentioning it. | `4` |\n38\t| 24 | `originator_account` | str | Earliest-dating strong account that mentioned it. | `photonbull` |\n39\t| 25 | `amplifier_accounts` | str | Strong accounts mentioning it after the originator, `;`-joined. | `ckcapitalxx;rjccapital` |\n40\t| 26 | `final_score_100` | int | Clamped 0–100 score from the rubric in `SCORING.md`. | `73` |\n41\t\n42\t### Wait — that's 26 columns above but the spec lists a few more derived ones.\n43\tThe full required set (matching the original request) is below; the table above\n44\tis the scoring core, and the following are **additional required columns**\n45\tappended after `final_score_100`:\n46\t\n47\t| # | Column | Type | Definition | Example |\n48\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n49\t| 27 | `watchlist_priority` | str | `High` (≥60) / `Med` (35–59) / `Low` (<35). | `High` |\n50\t| 28 | `actionable_comment` | str | Short templated comment summarising the signal. | `Multi-account memory play; earnings catalyst.` |\n51\t| 29 | `last_updated` | str (ISO) | Run timestamp (UTC). | `2026-07-13T...` |\n52\t\n53\t> Total required columns: **29** (the original 26 requested + the 3 derived\n54\t> ones that were always part of the requested list: `watchlist_priority`,\n55\t> `actionable_comment`, `last_updated`). The future script will emit exactly\n56\t> these column names in this order.\n57\t\n58\t---\n59\t\n60\t## Notes\n61\t\n62\t- All booleans are written as `True`/`False` (Python str of bool) for CSV\n63\t  portability; consumers should parse case-insensitively.\n64\t- Empty / unknown fields are written as empty strings, never `NaN`, so the CSV\n65\t  stays grep-friendly.\n66\t- `last_updated` uses UTC ISO-8601.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80a42da3-70a5-4179-95d8-64a5724a163e","uuid":"f5ba63fb-cf38-4b53-b825-b18e206c17e5","timestamp":"2026-09-23T16:58:30.591Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/3n/cp7h29p55gzds1ttv9rkjdgw0000gn/T/v3-TR_TICKER_INTELLIGENCE_V1-nwaodvq5/docs/TICKER_SCHEMA.md","content":"# docs/TICKER_SCHEMA.md\n\nColumn dictionary for the planned `data/state/master_tickers.csv` (produced by\n`build_master_tickers.py`). **No file exists yet** — this is the contract the\nfuture script will write.\n\nOne row per distinct ticker across all `data/exports/*_clean.csv` files.\n\n---\n\n## Columns (26)\n\n| # | Column | Type | Definition | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `ticker` | str | Uppercased ticker symbol, `$` stripped, deduped. | `MU` |\n| 2 | `main_theme` | str | Most common theme across this ticker's posts (see `SCORING.md`). | `memory` |\n| 3 | `sub_theme` | str | Second most common theme (or empty). | `AI infra` |\n| 4 | `accounts_mentioning` | int | Total distinct accounts (strong + other) that mentioned it. | `4` |\n| 5 | `mentions_photonbull` | int | # posts by `photonbull` mentioning it. | `3` |\n| 6 | `mentions_ckcapitalxx` | int | # posts by `ckcapitalxx`. | `2` |\n| 7 | `mentions_bryzonx` | int | # posts by `bryzonx`. | `0` |\n| 8 | `mentions_frenchie` | int | # posts by `frenchie`. | `1` |\n| 9 | `mentions_rjccapital` | int | # posts by `rjccapital`. | `5` |\n| 10 | `mentions_other_accounts` | int | # posts by accounts not in the strong set. | `2` |\n| 11 | `total_mentions` | int | Total posts (across all accounts) mentioning it. | `13` |\n| 12 | `recent_mentions_7d` | int | Posts in the last 7 days (vs run date). | `2` |\n| 13 | `recent_mentions_30d` | int | Posts in the last 30 days. | `6` |\n| 14 | `avg_engagement` | float | Mean per-post `engagement_score` for this ticker. | `42.7` |\n| 15 | `max_engagement` | int | Max single-post `engagement_score`. | `311` |\n| 16 | `dominant_post_type` | str | Modal `post_type_guess` (`original`/`reply`/`retweet`/`quote`). | `original` |\n| 17 | `conviction_global_1_to_5` | int | 1–5 conviction blend (thesis + recency + engagement). | `4` |\n| 18 | `short_term_signal` | bool | Any post flagged `short_term_signal`. | `True` |\n| 19 | `long_term_thesis` | bool | Any post flagged `long_term_thesis`. | `True` |\n| 20 | `catalyst` | bool | Any post has `has_catalyst_language`. | `True` |\n| 21 | `thesis_one_liner` | str | Best single representative post text (truncated). | `HBM cycle + MU earnings ...` |\n| 22 | `convergence_level` | int | 1–5 from distinct strong-account count (see `SCORING.md`). | `4` |\n| 23 | `signal_independence` | int | Distinct accounts (all) mentioning it. | `4` |\n| 24 | `originator_account` | str | Earliest-dating strong account that mentioned it. | `photonbull` |\n| 25 | `amplifier_accounts` | str | Strong accounts mentioning it after the originator, `;`-joined. | `ckcapitalxx;rjccapital` |\n| 26 | `final_score_100` | int | Clamped 0–100 score from the rubric in `SCORING.md`. | `73` |\n\n### Wait — that's 26 columns above but the spec lists a few more derived ones.\nThe full required set (matching the original request) is below; the table above\nis the scoring core, and the following are **additional required columns**\nappended after `final_score_100`:\n\n| # | Column | Type | Definition | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 27 | `watchlist_priority` | str | `High` (≥60) / `Med` (35–59) / `Low` (<35). | `High` |\n| 28 | `actionable_comment` | str | Short templated comment summarising the signal. | `Multi-account memory play; earnings catalyst.` |\n| 29 | `last_updated` | str (ISO) | Run timestamp (UTC). | `2026-07-13T...` |\n\n> Total required columns: **29** (the original 26 requested + the 3 derived\n> ones that were always part of the requested list: `watchlist_priority`,\n> `actionable_comment`, `last_updated`). The future script will emit exactly\n> these column names in this order.\n\n---\n\n## Notes\n\n- All booleans are written as `True`/`False` (Python str of bool) for CSV\n  portability; consumers should parse case-insensitively.\n- Empty / unknown fields are written as empty strings, never `NaN`, so the CSV\n  stays grep-friendly.\n- `last_updated` uses UTC ISO-8601.\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
